Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety §§ 5-301 through 5-314): That Section(s) 5–301 through 5–314 and the subtitle “Subtitle 3. Handgun Permits” of Article – Public Safety of the Annotated Code of Maryland be repealed.
Section 2 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-203): (i) A PERSON UNDER THE AGE OF 21 YEARS MAY NOT wear, carry, or transport a handgun, whether concealed or open, on or about the person; (ii) A PERSON UNDER THE AGE OF 21 YEARS MAY NOT wear, carry, or knowingly transport a handgun, whether concealed or open, in a vehicle traveling on a road or parking lot generally used by the public, highway, waterway, or airway of the State; (iii) A PERSON MAY NOT WEAR, CARRY, OR TRANSPORT A HANDGUN, WHETHER CONCEALED OR OPEN, ON OR ABOUT THE PERSON while on public school property in the State; (iv) A PERSON MAY NOT WEAR, CARRY, OR TRANSPORT A HANDGUN, WHETHER CONCEALED OR OPEN, ON OR ABOUT THE PERSON with the deliberate purpose of injuring or killing another person;
Section 2 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-207): (A) A PERSON MAY NOT WEAR, CARRY, OR TRANSPORT A HANDGUN WHILE THE PERSON IS UNDER THE INFLUENCE OF ALCOHOL OR DRUGS. (B) A PERSON WHO VIOLATES THIS SECTION IS GUILTY OF A MISDEMEANOR AND ON CONVICTION IS SUBJECT TO IMPRISONMENT NOT EXCEEDING 1 YEAR OR A FINE NOT EXCEEDING $1,000 OR BOTH.
